<title>USA: CME to widen stock futures trading limits - WSJ.</title>
<headline>CME to widen stock futures trading limits - WSJ.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-12-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange has proposed widening the trading limits on stock index futures, The Wall Street Journal reported Monday.</p>
<p>The proposed widening of the CME's collars is expected to sharply reduce the number of trading interruptions, the story says.</p>
<p>CME's trigger points are being touched off almost weekly, the story said.</p>
</text>
